From c89ba20e68c20e6adb83f0aa4db670e0275d6b7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 10:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix protect_elo_fields bypass for SECURITY DEFINER RPCs

The protect_elo_fields trigger blocked all ELO updates because
auth.uid() returns NULL in SQL Editor context and returns a non-admin
user ID when called from RPCs. Added session-variable bypass
(app.bypass_elo_protection) that is set by trusted SECURITY DEFINER
functions (recalc, apply_elo, admin_adjust) and auto-resets per
transaction. Direct user manipulation is still blocked.

https://claude.ai/code/session_01UJHkwU6DtKxG9A2TXhpVSB
---
 supabase/sql/critical_fixes_2026_04_15.sql | 285 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 267 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/supabase/sql/critical_fixes_2026_04_15.sql b/supabase/sql/critical_fixes_2026_04_15.sql
index e96bbe5..e412022 100644
--- a/supabase/sql/critical_fixes_2026_04_15.sql
+++ b/supabase/sql/critical_fixes_2026_04_15.sql
@@ -3,9 +3,50 @@
 -- Kør disse i rækkefølge i Supabase SQL Editor
 -- ============================================================================
 
